; Draw the lives still in reserve as small walking Willys
;
; Draws one 16x16 Willy sprite for each life left in #R$85CC (none when it is
; 0), from the left end of the bottom status row (screen row 21, column 0), two
; columns apart. All figures show the same walking frame of the right-facing
; Willy sprites (#R$9D00): frame = bits 2-3 of the tune step counter #R$85E1,
; so the row of figures walks on the spot, changing frame every 4 steps of the
; counter. The counter only advances while the tune is on, so with the tune off
; the figures stand still (observed). The figures are drawn straight onto the
; screen, not into the screen buffer, once per pass of the frame loop; their
; colours are the status bar attributes (#R$9A00), which are never rewritten
; by the loop.
; .
; The game starts with 7 figures. A death (#R$8B07) removes one after the death
; flash; when none is left, the next death is the game over.
; .
; Hardware: writes the screen bitmap.
@equ=LIVES_SCREEN=$50A0
@label=DrawLives
c$898B LD A,($85CC)  ; lives in reserve
 $898E LD HL,$50A0   ;
 $8991 OR A          ;
 $8992 RET Z         ; none: nothing to draw
 $8993 LD B,A        ; B = figures left to draw
@label=DrawLives_Loop
*$8994 LD C,$00      ; DrawSprite mode 0: replace
 $8996 PUSH HL       ;
 $8997 PUSH BC       ;
 $8998 LD A,($85E1)  ;
 $899B RLCA          ;
 $899C RLCA          ;
 $899D RLCA          ;
@isub=AND LIFE_FRAME_MASK
 $899E AND $60       ; frame offset 0, $20, $40 or $60 from bits 2-3
 $89A0 LD E,A        ;
@isub=LD D,WILLY_SPRITE_PAGE
 $89A1 LD D,$9D      ; DE = Willy facing right, frame 0-3
 $89A3 CALL $9456    ;
 $89A6 POP BC        ;
 $89A7 POP HL        ;
 $89A8 INC HL        ; next figure two columns to the right
 $89A9 INC HL        ;
 $89AA DJNZ $8994    ;
 $89AC RET           ;
